.TH VM-CONFIG 5 "2026" "vm-manager" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
vm-config \- configuration file for vm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vm/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
The configuration file for
.BR vm (1)
is optional. Where
.I XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is not set, it is
.IR ~/.config/vm/config.toml .
An absent file, and any setting it leaves out, takes the default. A file that
cannot be read, is not TOML, or names a setting not listed here is reported as
an error rather than ignored, so a misspelt setting is not silently without
effect.
.PP
It is TOML: one
.IR key " = " value
per line, with strings in double quotes and
.BR true " or " false
for the rest.
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
.BR catalogue_url " (string)"
The archive
.B vm update
fetches the catalogue from, a gzipped tar. The default is the project's own
repository on GitHub.
.TP
.BR catalogue_path " (string)"
The directory within that archive holding the catalogue entries. Default
.BR catalogue .
Set both this and
.B catalogue_url
to run a catalogue kept on an internal server.
.TP
.BR auto_pull " (boolean)"
Whether
.B vm run
fetches an image that is not already held. Default
.BR true .
With
.BR false ,
an image that is not held is an error unless
.B \-\-pull
says otherwise.
.TP
.BR add_ssh_config " (boolean)"
Whether
.B vm run
gives a machine an entry that lets plain
.BR ssh (1),
.BR scp (1)
and
.BR rsync (1)
reach it by name, as though
.B \-\-add\-ssh\-config
had been given. Default
.BR false .
.B \-\-no\-ssh\-config
turns it off for one machine, and an image that takes no cloud-init seed has no
account to reach, so it gets no entry. This setting is read by
.B vm run
only: a machine that already exists keeps what it was given, and
.B vm start
changes it with
.B \-\-add\-ssh\-config
or
.BR \-\-no\-ssh\-config .
.SH EXAMPLE
.RS
.nf
catalogue_url = "https://mirror.example.com/vm/catalogue.tar.gz"
catalogue_path = "catalogue"
auto_pull = false
add_ssh_config = true
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vm (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
